    "sentence_translations": [
      "Reach 100, Get 20 Off",
      "",
      "Little Le and Paul were out window-shopping for clothes.",
      "A lot of shop owners ran campaigns and had written: Reach 88, get 10 off. Reach 100, get 20 off.",
      "In other words, buy for at least 88 yuan and get a 10 yuan discount. Buy for at least 100 yuan and get a 20 yuan discount.",
      "",
      "Little Le looked and looked, and suddenly seemed unhappy.",
      "Paul asked what was wrong, and she said:",
      "“Sigh, why can’t my body weight be ‘Reach 88, lose 10. Reach 100, lose 20.’ Then I would never go over 50 kg!”",
      "",
      "Paul laughed: “Haha! Your weight is like charging your phone credit.”",
      "“Don’t they often have ‘charge 100, get 20 extra’ when you charge your phone credit?”"
    ]
  }
